To reduce background noise and echoes in the React SDK, you can use the audioConstraints option when connecting to EVI (1). These constraints are automatically enabled by default, but you can customize them if needed.

Good news: Echo cancellation and noise suppression are enabled by default! The React SDK automatically sets:
`echoCancellation: true` - Reduces echo from the input
`noiseSuppression: true` - Suppresses background noise
`autoGainControl: true` - Automatically adjusts microphone gain

Here's how you can explicitly configure these settings when connecting:

```import { useVoice } from '@humeai/voice-react';

export function StartCall({ accessToken }: { accessToken: string }) {
  const { connect } = useVoice();

  return (
    <button
      onClick={() => {
        void connect({
          auth: { type: 'accessToken', value: accessToken },
          configId: '<YOUR_CONFIG_ID>',
          audioConstraints: {
            echoCancellation: true,    // Reduce echo (default: true)
            noiseSuppression: true,    // Suppress background noise (default: true)
            autoGainControl: true      // Auto-adjust microphone gain (default: true)
          }
        });
      }}
    >
      Start Call
    </button>
  );
}```


Additional audio quality improvements:

The React SDK also uses AudioWorklet for better audio quality by default (1). If you experience performance issues on older browsers (like Safari 17.5), you can disable it:

```<VoiceProvider enableAudioWorklet={false}>
  {/* Your components */}
</VoiceProvider>```


These audio processing features work at the browser level and should significantly improve your audio quality with minimal configuration required!
